{"bug":"K002","report":"D","v":"partial","ref":"9. Invalid datetime formats panic","evidence":"“`datetime('%Q')`, `datetime_utc('%')`, and `--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'` each panicked” identifies the invalid-format builtin panics, but does not identify format(...).to_string() on a fallible Chrono formatter as the cause."}
{"bug":"K006","report":"A","v":"partial","ref":"2. Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning errors","evidence":"“`--timestamp --timestamp-format %Q` each panic” identifies the timestamp-format panic and cites src/config.rs:137, but does not identify format(...).to_string() on a fallible Chrono formatter as the cause."}
{"bug":"K008","report":"C","v":"missed","ref":"3. Two module names loading the same file share an execution identity","evidence":"“The compiler caches the parsed source solely by file path” concerns shared module identity. The report does not identify an external module ambiguity panic from unwrapping strip_prefix(parent)."}
{"bug":"K009","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"7. User-defined functions discard module bindings and invocation context","evidence":"“Referencing one backtick-backed global directly and through two function calls executes its backtick three times.” This concerns repeated assignment evaluation; the report does not identify shell() executing during --dry-run or its missing dry_run check."}
{"bug":"K010","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"8. Relative and unnormalized search ceilings are ignored","evidence":"“An absolute ceiling containing `child/../child` behaves likewise.” This concerns search-ceiling comparisons, not unnormalized module paths bypassing cycle detection and repeating compilation until the OS path length limit."}
